// Destruction (WP5.5, docs/rules/destruction.md): what is shot to zero leaves the world. Two stories on the
// 96 by 64 cell map of the `pathing` scenario (assets/maps/pathing; the rock wall x 70..71, rows 27..63, with
// two gaps, rows 44..47 and rows 56..59, east of the river), with explicit attack orders only (no automatic
// targeting: what happens is what is written here). `combat: true` gives the world the weapons, `destruction:
// true` the death stage; the settings are the simulation's own (the numbers of sim.ron: a vehicle wreck lies
// 600 ticks, rubble 1200).
//
// 1. THE GAP. Two structures close each gap of the wall (relay_transmitter, 2 by 2 cells, 400 hit points):
//    slots 0 and 1 the first gap, slots 2 and 3 the second. Three light tanks (4, 5, 6) stand five cells west
//    of the first gap, in reach of it, and shoot its two structures down. When they fall their cells are free,
//    the routes over them are rebuilt, and a rifleman (slot 7), for whom the east bank was a walk of some 130
//    cells round the lake while both gaps were shut (the wall ends at the lake), is sent there afterwards and
//    walks through the gap that was a wall of structures. The second gap stays shut. The rubble of the two
//    structures lies where they stood and goes after 1200 ticks.
//
// 2. THE WRECK. Two light tanks and two riflemen (8, 9, 10, 11 of owner 0) against four rocket troopers
//    (12 to 15 of owner 1). The troopers all fire at the first tank (8), which fires back; the riflemen shoot
//    a trooper. The tank is destroyed and leaves a wreck for 600 ticks; a trooper that falls leaves nothing.
//    The kill goes to the shooter that did the most damage in the tick the victim fell, the others who hit
//    it that tick are assists, ties by where they stood.
//
// CI runs it on Linux and Windows and requires the checksum in destruction.expected;
// tools/sf_headless/tests/destruction.rs asserts the story along the run.
//
// `unit_defs` names a FROZEN copy of the shipped definitions (tanks_vs_infantry_defs/, the set of WP5.4), so a
// rebalance of assets/config/ does not move this checksum.
//
// Entity ids, all at generation 0, in the order the spawns are written. Owners: 0 Meridian, 1 Veyran.
//    0  relay_transmitter (32, 400 hp)  owner 1  cell (70, 44)   the first gap, north half
//    1  relay_transmitter               owner 1  cell (70, 46)   the first gap, south half
//    2  relay_transmitter               owner 1  cell (70, 56)   the second gap, north half
//    3  relay_transmitter               owner 1  cell (70, 58)   the second gap, south half
//    4  light_tank (19, 400 hp)         owner 0  cell (65, 44)   attacks 0
//    5  light_tank                      owner 0  cell (65, 46)   attacks 0
//    6  light_tank                      owner 0  cell (65, 48)   attacks 1
//    7  rifleman (12)                   owner 0  cell (62, 50)   moves to (90, 46) at tick 800
//    8  light_tank                      owner 0  cell (20, 50)   attacks 13
//    9  light_tank                      owner 0  cell (20, 52)   attacks 12
//   10  rifleman                        owner 0  cell (21, 48)   attacks 12
//   11  rifleman                        owner 0  cell (21, 54)   attacks 12
//   12 to 15  rocket_trooper (13)       owner 1  cells (26, 48) to (26, 51)   attack 8
Scenario(
    name: "destruction",
    seed: 0x0D57_0055,
    map: (width: 96, height: 64),
    map_name: Some("pathing"),
    unit_defs: Some("tanks_vs_infantry_defs"),
    combat: true,
    destruction: true,
    ticks: 2000,
    commands: [
        // --- the gaps, shut ---
        (tick: 0, command: PlaceStructure(kind: 32, owner: 1, cell: (70, 44))),
        (tick: 0, command: PlaceStructure(kind: 32, owner: 1, cell: (70, 46))),
        (tick: 0, command: PlaceStructure(kind: 32, owner: 1, cell: (70, 56))),
        (tick: 0, command: PlaceStructure(kind: 32, owner: 1, cell: (70, 58))),

        // --- the three tanks and the rifleman west of the wall ---
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 19, owner: 0, cell: (65, 44))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 19, owner: 0, cell: (65, 46))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 19, owner: 0, cell: (65, 48))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 12, owner: 0, cell: (62, 50))),

        // --- the fight: two tanks and two riflemen against four rocket troopers ---
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 19, owner: 0, cell: (20, 50))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 19, owner: 0, cell: (20, 52))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 12, owner: 0, cell: (21, 48))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 12, owner: 0, cell: (21, 54))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 13, owner: 1, cell: (26, 48))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 13, owner: 1, cell: (26, 49))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 13, owner: 1, cell: (26, 50))),
        (tick: 0, command: SpawnUnit(kind: 13, owner: 1, cell: (26, 51))),

        // --- the orders ---
        (tick: 1, command: OrderAttack(ids: [Id(4, 0), Id(5, 0)], target: (0, 0))),
        (tick: 1, command: OrderAttack(ids: [Id(6, 0)], target: (1, 0))),
        (tick: 1, command: OrderAttack(ids: [Id(8, 0)], target: (13, 0))),
        (tick: 1, command: OrderAttack(ids: [Id(9, 0), Id(10, 0), Id(11, 0)], target: (12, 0))),
        (tick: 1, command: OrderAttack(ids: [Id(12, 0), Id(13, 0), Id(14, 0), Id(15, 0)], target: (8, 0))),
        (tick: 800, command: OrderMove(ids: [Id(7, 0)], target: (90, 46))),
    ],
)
